Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20200707060601.31907-2-peter.chen@kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was rooted in the fact that the initial call to the interrupt handler (`ci_irq`) was made during the extcon notifier, which successfully woke up the controller but did not handle any pending events. This left the extcon use case malfunctioning when the controller resumed from a low power state, as it needed additional handling to respond to subsequent extcon-related events.

Here is the patch:
